known_for_template:
Each answer below replies to "What is {brand} known for?". For each answer, list what it says {brand} is known for, in the order the answer raises them, and map each point to exactly one of these themes: {themes}. Use "{fallback}" for a buyer-facing point no theme fits. Skip company facts such as funding, ownership, valuation or history. Give each point a short exact quote from the answer. At most {max_items} points per answer.

Return JSON: {"answers":[{"answer":1,"points":[{"theme":"","quote":""}]}]}

{answers}

objection_template:
Each answer below replies to "Why might someone not choose {brand}?". For each answer, list every reason it gives, in the order the answer raises them, with a short exact quote. Put each reason in one group. Existing groups: {groups}. Use an existing group's exact name whenever the reason means the same thing; name a new group (2 to 5 words, plain buyer wording) only for a reason no existing group covers, and reuse that new name for every reason with the same meaning. At most {max_items} reasons per answer.

Return JSON: {"answers":[{"answer":1,"reasons":[{"group":"","quote":""}]}]}

{answers}

theme_template:
Each answer below replies to "{question}". For each answer, list every brand or business it names as an option, in the order first named, exactly as written. At most {max_items} names per answer.

Return JSON: {"answers":[{"answer":1,"brands":[""]}]}

{answers}
